Text>How the figures of both reports are formed; text only.</Text><TextBrush>[90:90:90]</TextBrush><TextOptions>,,,,WordWrap=True,A=0</TextOptions><VertAlignment>Center</VertAlignment></method_Subtitle></Components><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><DataSourceName>ScriptedReportMeta</DataSourceName><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Filters isList="true" count="0" /><Name>method_TitleBand</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="589" /><Sort isList="true" count="0" /></method_TitleBand><MethodLevels_Band Ref="594" type="DataBand" isKey="true"><Brush>Transparent</Brush><BusinessObjectGuid isNull="true" /><CanBreak>False</CanBreak><ClientRectangle>0,3.55,26.7,1.7</ClientRectangle><Components isList="true" count="1"><MethodLevels_Text Ref="595" type="Text" isKey="true"><Border>All;[190:195:205];0.5;Solid;False;4;Black</Border><Brush>[247:248:250]</Brush><CanGrow>True</CanGrow><ClientRectangle>0.2,0.1,26.3,1.5</ClientRectangle><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Font>Segoe UI,9</Font><Margins>0.3,0.3,0.1,0.1</Margins><Name>MethodLevels_Text</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="594" /><Text>Levels. n-0 is the quasi-dynamic simulation (QDS) of the base network without planned outages. n-1 is the contingency analysis of the base network at the study times inside each case's outage windows. (n-1)' is the same contingency analysis with the case's planned outages active. Planned outages are active only on the scenario side.</Text><TextBrush>[55:55:55]</TextBrush><TextOptions>,,,,WordWrap=True,A=0</TextOptions><VertAlignment>Center</VertAlignment></MethodLevels_Text></Components><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><DataSourceName>ScriptedReportMeta</DataSourceName><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Filters isList="true" count="0" /><Name>MethodLevels_Band</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="589" /><Sort isList="true" count="0" /></MethodLevels_Band><MethodComparison_Band Ref="596" type="DataBand" isKey="true"><Brush>Transparent</Brush><BusinessObjectGuid isNull="true" /><CanBreak>False</CanBreak><ClientRectangle>0,5.35,26.7,1.7</ClientRectangle><Components isList="true" count="1"><MethodComparison_Text Ref="597" type="Text" isKey="true"><Border>All;[190:195:205];0.5;Solid;False;4;Black</Border><Brush>[247:248:250]</Brush><CanGrow>True</CanGrow><ClientRectangle>0.2,0.1,26.3,1.5</ClientRectangle><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Font>Segoe UI,9</Font><Margins>0.3,0.3,0.1,0.1</Margins><Name>MethodComparison_Text</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="596" /><Text>Comparison. (n-1)' is compared with n-1 only for the same study time, contingency, element, criterion and post-fault phase, with the same limit. NEW: only the scenario violates the limit. WORSENED: both violate and the scenario by more than the tolerance. PRE-EXISTING: both violate within the tolerance. IMPROVED: both violate and the scenario by less than the tolerance. RESOLVED: only n-1 violates. OK: neither. A value exactly on the limit is no violation.</Text><TextBrush>[55:55:55]</TextBrush><TextOptions>,,,,WordWrap=True,A=0</TextOptions><VertAlignment>Center</VertAlignment></MethodComparison_Text></Components><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><DataSourceName>ScriptedReportMeta</DataSourceName><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Filters isList="true" count="0" /><Name>MethodComparison_Band</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="589" /><Sort isList="true" count="0" /></MethodComparison_Band><MethodQuality_Band Ref="598" type="DataBand" isKey="true"><Brush>Transparent</Brush><BusinessObjectGuid isNull="true" /><CanBreak>False</CanBreak><ClientRectangle>0,7.15,26.7,1.7</ClientRectangle><Components isList="true" count="1"><MethodQuality_Text Ref="599" type="Text" isKey="true"><Border>All;[190:195:205];0.5;Solid;False;4;Black</Border><Brush>[247:248:250]</Brush><CanGrow>True</CanGrow><ClientRectangle>0.2,0.1,26.3,1.5</ClientRectangle><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Font>Segoe UI,9</Font><Margins>0.3,0.3,0.1,0.1</Margins><Name>MethodQuality_Text</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="598" /><Text>Quality. FAILED (no result where one was expected), NOT EVALUATED (a study time or value is missing or a value inside the recording limits does not prove the limit), NOT APPLICABLE (the contingency's equipment is already switched off by the case) and NOT COMPARABLE (different limits) never count as OK. Equipment switched off by the case is no finding.</Text><TextBrush>[55:55:55]</TextBrush><TextOptions>,,,,WordWrap=True,A=0</TextOptions><VertAlignment>Center</VertAlignment></MethodQuality_Text></Components><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><DataSourceName>ScriptedReportMeta</DataSourceName><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Filters isList="true" count="0" /><Name>MethodQuality_Band</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="589" /><Sort isList="true" count="0" /></MethodQuality_Band><MethodCounting_Band Ref="600" type="DataBand" isKey="true"><Brush>Transparent</Brush><BusinessObjectGuid isNull="true" /><CanBreak>False</CanBreak><ClientRectangle>0,8.95,26.7,1.7</ClientRectangle><Components isList="true" count="1"><MethodCounting_Text Ref="601" type="Text" isKey="true"><Border>All;[190:195:205];0.5;Solid;False;4;Black</Border><Brush>[247:248:250]</Brush><CanGrow>True</CanGrow><ClientRectangle>0.2,0.1,26.3,1.5</ClientRectangle><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Font>Segoe UI,9</Font><Margins>0.3,0.3,0.1,0.1</Margins><Name>MethodCounting_Text</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="600" /><Text>Counting. Elements are distinct equipment; findings are single cells of study time x contingency x element x criterion. A finding category can hold the same element as another, so element counts are not added. Episodes are consecutive examined study times with the same finding; the time between study times is no proof of a continuous violation.</Text><TextBrush>[55:55:55]</TextBrush><TextOptions>,,,,WordWrap=True,A=0</TextOptions><VertAlignment>Center</VertAlignment></MethodCounting_Text></Components><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><DataSourceName>ScriptedReportMeta</DataSourceName><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Filters isList="true" count="0" /><Name>MethodCounting_Band</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="589" /><Sort isList="true" count="0" /></MethodCounting_Band><MethodExtremes_Band Ref="602" type="DataBand" isKey="true"><Brush>Transparent</Brush><BusinessObjectGuid isNull="true" /><CanBreak>False</CanBreak><ClientRectangle>0,10.75,26.7,1.7</ClientRectangle><Components isList="true" count="1"><MethodExtremes_Text Ref="603" type="Text" isKey="true"><Border>All;[190:195:205];0.5;Solid;False;4;Black</Border><Brush>[247:248:250]</Brush><CanGrow>True</CanGrow><ClientRectangle>0.2,0.1,26.3,1.5</ClientRectangle><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Font>Segoe UI,9</Font><Margins>0.3,0.3,0.1,0.1</Margins><Name>MethodExtremes_Text</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="602" /><Text>Extremes and changes. The absolute extremes of n-1 and (n-1)' are formed independently and may lie at different times and contingencies; they are never subtracted. The coincident change comes only from a same-time pair.</Text><TextBrush>[55:55:55]</TextBrush><TextOptions>,,,,WordWrap=True,A=0</TextOptions><VertAlignment>Center</VertAlignment></MethodExtremes_Text></Components><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><DataSourceName>ScriptedReportMeta</DataSourceName><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Filters isList="true" count="0" /><Name>MethodExtremes_Band</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="589" /><Sort isList="true" count="0" /></MethodExtremes_Band><MethodColours_Band Ref="604" type="DataBand" isKey="true"><Brush>Transparent</Brush><BusinessObjectGuid isNull="true" /><CanBreak>False</CanBreak><ClientRectangle>0,12.55,26.7,1.7</ClientRectangle><Components isList="true" count="1"><MethodColours_Text Ref="605" type="Text" isKey="true"><Border>All;[190:195:205];0.5;Solid;False;4;Black</Border><Brush>[247:248:250]</Brush><CanGrow>True</CanGrow><ClientRectangle>0.2,0.1,26.3,1.5</ClientRectangle><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Font>Segoe UI,9</Font><Margins>0.3,0.3,0.1,0.1</Margins><Name>MethodColours_Text</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="604" /><Text>Colours. Red rows hold NEW or WORSENED findings, yellow rows other violations or quality statuses; every status is also written as text.</Text><TextBrush>[55:55:55]</TextBrush><TextOptions>,,,,WordWrap=True,A=0</TextOptions><VertAlignment>Center</VertAlignment></MethodColours_Text></Components><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><DataSourceName>ScriptedReportMeta</DataSourceName><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Filters isList="true" count="0" /><Name>MethodColours_Band</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="589" /><Sort isList="true" count="0" /></MethodColours_Band><MethodLimits_Band Ref="606" type="DataBand" isKey="true"><Brush>Transparent</Brush><BusinessObjectGuid isNull="true" /><CanBreak>False</CanBreak><ClientRectangle>0,14.35,26.7,1.7</ClientRectangle><Components isList="true" count="1"><MethodLimits_Text Ref="607" type="Text" isKey="true"><Border>All;[190:195:205];0.5;Solid;False;4;Black</Border><Brush>[247:248:250]</Brush><CanGrow>True</CanGrow><ClientRectangle>0.2,0.1,26.3,1.5</ClientRectangle><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Font>Segoe UI,9</Font><Margins>0.3,0.3,0.1,0.1</Margins><Name>MethodLimits_Text</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="606" /><Text>Limitations. This pre-assessment is no release and no proof of n-1 security, security of supply, protection coordination or safe isolation.</Text><TextBrush>[55:55:55]</TextBrush><TextOptions>,,,,WordWrap=True,A=0</TextOptions><VertAlignment>Center</VertAlignment></MethodLimits_Text></Components><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><DataSourceName>ScriptedReportMeta</DataSourceName><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Filters isList="true" count="0" /><Name>MethodLimits_Band</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="589" /><Sort isList="true" count="0" /></MethodLimits_Band><BandPageFooter_Method Ref="1149" type="PageFooterBand" isKey="true"><Brush>Transparent</Brush><ClientRectangle>0,17.700000000000003,26.7,0.9</ClientRectangle><Components isList="true" count="3"><FooterRule_Method Ref="1150" type="Text" isKey="true"><Border>Top;[155:155:155];0.5;Solid;False;4;Black</Border><Brush>Transparent</Brush><ClientRectangle>0,0,26.7,0.15</ClientRectangle><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Font>Segoe UI,9</Font><Margins>0.12,0.12,0,0</Margins><Name>FooterRule_Method</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="1149" /><Text></Text><TextBrush>[55:55:55]</TextBrush><TextOptions>,,,,WordWrap=True,A=0</TextOptions><VertAlignment>Center</VertAlignment></FooterRule_Method><FooterLeft_Method Ref="1151" type="Text" isKey="true"><Border>None;Transparent;0;None;False;4;Black</Border><Brush>Transparent</Brush><ClientRectangle>0,0.15,16.0,0.75</ClientRectangle><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Font>Segoe UI,7.5</Font><Margins>0.12,0.12,0,0</Margins><Name>FooterLeft_Method</Name><Page isRef="589" /><Parent isRef="1149" /><Text>PRE-ASSESSMENT | NOT FOR OPERATIONAL USE</Text><TextBrush>[90:90:90]</TextBrush><TextOptions>,,,,WordWrap=True,A=0</TextOptions><VertAlignment>Center</VertAlignment></FooterLeft_Method><FooterRight_Method Ref="1152" type="Text" isKey="true"><Border>None;Transparent;0;None;False;4;Black</Border><Brush>Transparent</Brush><ClientRectangle>20.7,0.15,6.0,0.75</ClientRectangle><Conditions isList="true" count="0" /><Expressions isList="true" count="0" /><Font>Segoe UI,7.5</Font><HorAlignment>Right</HorAlignment><Margins>0.12,0.12,0,0</Margins><Name>FooterRight_Method</Name><Page isRef="589" /